      "content": "It's incredibly heavy to carry such intense feelings, and you’re showing a lot of courage by voicing your struggles. It’s also okay to worry about what the future holds. But consider that being stuck in a loop of suffering is never a permanent state. Change takes time and effort, and many steps can lead to a better situation. A mental health professional can work with you to find coping strategies and might help change the trajectory of your life. Letting go of the idea that things can’t change is a massive barrier. Remember, both you and your loved ones, have the ability to find hope and ways to cope, even when the journey feels long and tough. Is there a specific aspect of therapy that you're unsure about or any particular fear you have about the process?",
